# Set to "false" to disable the walkthrough feature entirely in development
VITE_WALKTHROUGH_ENABLED=true
# --- API / backend ---------------------------------------------------------
# Base origin of the Django backend. Leave EMPTY when the app is served from the
# same origin as the API (the usual dev + prod setup): all requests are then
# relative to `/api/...`, which is what the Vite proxy targets below.
# Set it only when the API lives on a different host, e.g.:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com
VITE_API_URL=

# In production the SPA is mounted under the `/dashboard` basename (see
# src/routes/index.tsx and src/lib/api-client.ts). That means:
#   - the app is served from https://host/dashboard/
#   - API calls go to https://host/api/... (same origin, NOT /dashboard/api)
#   - auth cookies are set on the shared origin, so `withCredentials` works
#     without CORS/cookie-domain wrangling. Cross-origin deployments MUST set
#     VITE_API_URL *and* configure CORS + SameSite=None; Secure cookies.

# Dev proxy: Vite forwards `/api` to the Django dev server. Adjust the port in
# vite.config.ts if your backend does not listen on 8000.
#   server.proxy['/api'] = { target: 'http://127.0.0.1:8000', changeOrigin: true }